1.3 Example: GPS fuel and utilization monitoring
Assume one excavator:
Parameter	Illustrative value
Planned shift	10 hours
Engine running	8 hours
Productive operation	6.5 hours
Idle engine time	1.5 hours
Fuel consumption	112 litres
Production	520 m³

Calculations:
- Fuel consumption per engine hour = 112 ÷ 8 = 14 L/hr
- Fuel consumption per productive hour = 112 ÷ 6.5 = 17.23 L/productive hr
- Fuel consumption per cubic metre = 112 ÷ 520 = 0.215 L/m³
- Productive time percentage of engine running time = 6.5 ÷ 8 × 100 = 81.25%
The GPS report should be compared with the operator logbook, diesel issue register, HMR and actual measurement of production.

Management rule: GPS data is an independent control signal, not automatically proof of fuel theft or operator misconduct. Check sensor calibration, tank shape, vehicle inclination, refuelling records and data gaps first.
