2. P&M KPI management — detailed formulas
A KPI is a measurable indicator used to judge whether equipment is performing according to plan.
2.1 The main equipment KPIs
KPI	Formula	What it tells management
Mechanical availability	Available hours ÷ planned hours × 100	Equipment readiness
Utilization	Operating hours ÷ available hours × 100	How much available time is used
Productive utilization	Productive hours ÷ available hours × 100	How much time creates output
Productivity	Actual output ÷ productive hours	Actual production rate
Productivity achievement	Actual output ÷ planned output × 100	Performance against plan
MTBF	Operating hours ÷ number of failures	Reliability
MTTR	Repair hours ÷ number of failures	Repair efficiency
Fuel efficiency	Fuel consumed ÷ output	Fuel per unit of production
Maintenance cost ratio	Maintenance cost ÷ equipment operating cost × 100	Maintenance cost burden
Cost per unit	Total equipment cost ÷ actual output	Commercial efficiency

Define your denominator carefully. Companies sometimes use planned hours, scheduled hours or calendar hours differently. Standardise the definition across all projects before comparing KPI results.
