5.5 Breakdown troubleshooting method
Use a systematic approach, not random replacement of parts.
Troubleshooting flow
1. Confirm the complaint with the operator.
2. Check safety, machine condition and fault codes.
3. Check basic causes: oil, coolant, filters, wiring, connections, leaks.
4. Measure pressure, temperature, voltage, flow or other relevant parameters.
5. Compare with the exact OEM manual specifications.
6. Identify the root cause and confirm the repair method.
7. Repair, test under controlled conditions and record results.
8. Review repeat failure and preventive action.

