Tandem lifting: Two cranes lifting one load require an engineered lift plan. Load distribution, changing radius, centre of gravity, crane configuration and differential movement must be calculated. Never assume each crane automatically carries 50% of the load.
1.4 Hydraulic and pneumatic safety








dsic-hydraulic.en.made-in-china.com


Hydraulic equipment is common in:
- Excavators.
- Piling rigs.
- Crawler cranes.
- Launching girders.
- Hydraulic lifters.
- SPMT systems.
- Concrete pumps.
- Stressing jacks.
Main hazards:
- High-pressure oil injection.
- Hose burst.
- Cylinder movement.
- Accumulator pressure.
- Sudden pressure release.
- Unexpected lowering of raised equipment.
Safe maintenance sequence:
1. Park on stable ground.
2. Lower all attachments to a safe position.
3. Switch off the engine and isolate power.
4. Apply lockout/tagout.
5. Release stored hydraulic or pneumatic pressure according to the OEM procedure.
6. Mechanically support raised components with rated supports.
7. Verify zero-energy condition using an appropriate method.
8. Only then begin repair.
Never use your hand to find a hydraulic leak. Use an approved leak-detection method. High-pressure fluid injection injuries require immediate emergency medical treatment.

