7. Indian statutory and technical safety references
For an Indian construction project, your safety team should identify the exact legal requirements applicable to the project, establishment, equipment and work activity.

Important references include:
- The applicable provisions of the Building and Other Construction Workers legislation and rules.
- The applicable provisions of the Occupational Safety, Health and Working Conditions Code and commencement/rules, as relevant.
- Applicable Central and State electrical safety regulations and CEA safety regulations.
- Relevant BIS / IS standards.
- Applicable factory rules where the establishment is covered.
- OEM operating and maintenance manuals.
- Project-specific HSE requirements and approved lifting procedures.
Do not rely on a generic checklist as proof of statutory compliance. Verify the latest applicable law, rules, equipment certification, inspection intervals and competent-person requirements with your HSE and electrical engineering teams.

8. AGM / Head P&M responsibilities
Your role should include the following:
1. Establish mechanical and electrical inspection standards for every project.
2. Ensure machine-wise risk assessments and preventive maintenance.
3. Verify operator, mechanic and electrician competency.
4. Ensure LOTO and PTW compliance.
5. Review lifting plans and critical lifting operations.
6. Ensure crane, pressure-system and lifting-accessory inspection and certification.
7. Control electrical panels, earthing, protection and emergency stops.
8. Review safety-critical defects and prevent operation until safely rectified.
9. Audit workshops, stores, DG sets and plant installations.
10. Review incident investigation and root-cause corrective actions.
11. Maintain safety records, training and statutory compliance.
12. Report major risks and unresolved actions to senior management.
